.TH SIMPLE_SHELL 1 "February 2026" "1.0" "Simple Shell Manual"
.SH NAME
simple_shell \- a simple UNIX command line interpreter
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B simple_shell
.SH DESCRIPTION
Simple Shell is a basic UNIX command line interpreter that replicates basic functionalities of the sh shell. It reads commands from standard input and executes them.
.SH USAGE
The shell works in both interactive and non-interactive mode.
.PP
In interactive mode, run:
.PP
.RS
$ ./simple_shell
.RE
.PP
In non-interactive mode:
.PP
.RS
$ echo "command" | ./simple_shell
.RE
.SH COMMANDS
The following built-in commands are supported:
.PP
.B env
.RS
Prints the current environment variables
.RE
.PP
.B exit
.RS
Exits the shell
.RE
.SH EXAMPLES
.PP
Interactive mode:
.RS
$ ./simple_shell
.br
($) /bin/ls
.br
file1 file2 file3
.br
($) exit
.RE
.PP
Non-interactive mode:
.RS
$ echo "/bin/ls" | ./simple_shell
.br
file1 file2 file3
.RE
.SH SEE ALSO
sh(1), bash(1)
.SH BUGS
No known bugs.
